<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_PeakstormLight.xml   CRACKEDLANDS_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 §5 (mark 8, the herald sky)

  "Clear and dry here while the northern skyline flickers with the
  Contagion's storm (sky color + distant strike SFX; ZERO precipitation by
  construction - ban 5)."

  ZERO PRECIPITATION BY CONSTRUCTION: no rainRate / snowRate (WeatherDef
  defaults both to 0), no overlay/workers, and the only event maker is
  RM_WeatherEvent_DistantFlicker - a subclass of vanilla
  WeatherEvent_LightningFlash (read via RimSage 2026-09-29) at reduced
  brightness. The base class's FireEvent plays SoundDefOf.Thunder_OffMap:
  the distant strike, and nothing strikes the map (no
  WeatherEvent_LightningStrike maker here, unlike vanilla DryThunderstorm).

  Sky (CRACKEDLANDS_GPT_ENRICHMENT_1 §3, owner-picked): "the northern sky
  turns bruised red, distant lightning silhouettes the peaks". RimWorld's sky
  colour is one global colour, never directional, so "northern" is carried by
  the flicker and the description; the bruise is a red-violet cast that is
  faint at midday and deep at dusk and night. TUNED, every value: chosen to
  read as bruised, not as a fire or an eclipse, against Clear's own sets.

  Wind: "cool, wet-clay air pushes through the slots" - windSpeedFactor 1.6
  (TUNED: noticeably gusty, short of a storm's). The dust that briefly
  REVERSES is not expressible in a WeatherDef (no mote direction field);
  owed to CRACKEDLANDS_PEAKSTORM_DUST_REVERSAL_1.

  Flood coupling (RM_MapComponent_CanyonFlood): while this weather stands,
  the flood clock rolls ONCE per cycle (TUNED 0.6) to pull its next flood
  forward to 0.5-2 days out (setting "peakstormBiasEnabled") - the storm
  raises the odds without being a perfect timer.
-->
<Defs>

  <WeatherDef>
    <defName>RM_PeakstormLight</defName>
    <label>peakstorm light</label>
    <description>Clear and dry overhead, while the far skyline flickers and grumbles with a storm on the peaks upstream. Nothing falls here. The water it is making will arrive later, down the canyons.</description>
    <ambientSounds>
      <li>Ambient_Wind_Clear</li>
    </ambientSounds>
    <durationRange>10000~30000</durationRange>
    <windSpeedFactor>1.6</windSpeedFactor>
    <eventMakers>
      <li>
        <averageInterval>900</averageInterval>
        <eventClass>RimMandrake.FloodedCanyon.RM_WeatherEvent_DistantFlicker</eventClass>
      </li>
    </eventMakers>
    <favorability>Neutral</favorability>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <perceivePriority>1</perceivePriority>
    <repeatable>true</repeatable>
    <skyColorsDay>
      <sky>(1,0.93,0.92)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.73,0.70,0.74)</shadow>
      <overlay>(1,0.95,0.94)</overlay>
      <saturation>1.2</saturation>
    </skyColorsDay>
    <skyColorsDusk>
      <sky>(0.78,0.50,0.50)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.93,0.86,0.92)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.78,0.66,0.72)</overlay>
      <saturation>1.2</saturation>
    </skyColorsDusk>
    <skyColorsNightEdge>
      <sky>(0.50,0.36,0.46)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.92,0.88,0.92)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.58,0.48,0.56)</overlay>
      <saturation>1.15</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightEdge>
    <skyColorsNightMid>
      <sky>(0.44,0.34,0.46)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.85,0.82,0.86)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.54,0.46,0.56)</overlay>
      <saturation>1.15</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightMid>
  </WeatherDef>

</Defs>
